/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134367554,imgsize-1817443.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Atlanta teacher warned students away from locked 26-acre forest; $3 million may open it]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134365782.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[For years, Atlanta teacher Renette Scott warned students against entering the locked woods outside Therrell High School, unaware that the 26-acre forest was city-owned. After years of community advocacy, Atlanta secured a $2 million state grant and will add $1 million of its own to help turn Falling Water Park into a public park with trails, a lake boardwalk and wildlife education.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-atlanta-teacher-spent-years-warning-students-away-from-a-locked-26-acre-forest-outside-their-school-community-organizing-has-now-secured-3-million-to-begin-turning-the-hidden-city-land-into-a-public-park/articleshow/134365782.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-atlanta-teacher-spent-years-warning-students-away-from-a-locked-26-acre-forest-outside-their-school-community-organizing-has-now-secured-3-million-to-begin-turning-the-hidden-city-land-into-a-public-park/articleshow/134365782.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-20T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134365914,imgsize-173566.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[No sugar, no alcohol, 300 push-ups and 300 squats: Inside the lifestyle of Telegram CEO Pavel Durov]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134367271.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Tel