//timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/strong-6-1-magnitude-earthquake-strikes-papua-new-guinea-region/articleshow/134366256.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-20T15:13:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134366265,imgsize-1302059.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[West Virginia teen builds low-cost bionic hand, selected for national science competition]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134364866.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Kianoosh Nawai, an eighth-grader from West Virginia Virtual Academy, has been selected as the state’s only finalist in the 2026 Thermo Fisher Scientific Junior Innovators Challenge. He designed and built a low-cost 3D-printed prosthetic hand, testing its grip strength and finger movement. His project was selected from nearly 2,000 entrants and will compete against 29 other finalists in Washington, DC.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-kianoosh-nawai-the-west-virginia-eighth-grader-who-built-a-low-cost-3d-printed-bionic-hand-and-became-his-states-only-finalist-in-a-national-stem-contest/articleshow/134364866.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-kianoosh-nawai-the-west-virginia-eighth-grader-who-built-a-low-cost-3d-printed-bionic-hand-and-became-his-states-only-finalist-in-a-national-stem-contest/articleshow/134364866.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-20T15:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134365054,imgsize-59076.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1942, 24-year-old WWII pilot vanished over Egypt, 84 years later, his family finally buried him]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134364960.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After eight long decades, Captain Marvin Lancaster was laid to rest in North Carolina. His fighter plane was shot down over Egypt during WWII in 1942, and for years, his identity remained a mystery. Thanks to advanced DNA matching, his family finally received closure, gathering to remember his bravery and sacrifice on National POW MIA Recognition Day, a day dedicated to honoring the missing servicemen and women.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1942-a-24-year-old-wwii-pilot-vanished-over-egypt-84-years-later-his-family-finally-buries-him-beside-his-parents-in-north-carolina/articleshow/134364960.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1942-a-24-year-old-wwii-pilot-vanished-over-egypt-84-years-later-his-family-finally-buries-him-beside-his-parents-in-north-carolina/articleshow/134364960.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-20T15:04:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134365023,imgsize-851371.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1967 Rolex Daytona found in family drawer after 45 years sells for CHF 1.143 million in Geneva]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134364658.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A rare 1967 Rolex Daytona Reference 6239 in 18k yellow gold, fitted with a Paul Newman dial, has sold for CHF 1.143 million in Geneva. The watch had remained in the family of its original owner for more than 45 years before being inherited by two sisters. Sotheby’s had estimated it at CHF 300,000 to CHF 600,000.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-worl